      "message": "fix(motion): the rotary wrap closes a flatted bar's ragged seam and refuses an open mesh by name\n\nThe developed sheet's two free ends were closed by a meridian wall standing\nin the plane of the cover's extreme column. On a revolve the seam column is\nstraight and lies in that plane; on a bar with a D-flat across the seam the\nflat's vertices sit at their own azimuths, the seam column is ragged, and the\nwall met none of its edges - \"the mesh is open: 4/8/16 dangling chord ends\".\n\nNow each seam edge (an edge its two facets develop one period apart) hangs a\nvertical curtain down to the floor radius from its lower (first copy) and its\nupper (second copy) version - multiaxis::rotary_seam. On a revolve that is\nthe old wall, split on the same diagonal: the OffsetRings wrap digest is\nunchanged. The wrap also refuses an open mesh by name before developing it;\non main a hole no ladder level sliced through wrapped silently.\n\nPinned by rotary_dflat::{a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement,\na_bar_with_a_hole_in_its_skin_is_still_refused_by_name,\na_flat_channel_across_the_seam_is_refused_adaptive_by_name_and_rings_cut_it}\n(all three fail on main), the last being #9's seam law end to end.\n\nFixes #54\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
