      "message": "fix(motion): the rotary wrap refuses a feature across its seam by name instead of gouging\n\nPR #210's review: a D-flat across the wrap's seam (off its centre line)\nwrapped and put 12 to 1606 cut tips inside the part, down to the axis. The\ncover's ends read the metal another lap holds as air. Clipping the cover to\nthe ragged seam's inner columns removed that strip, but a whole-lap band at\nthe flat's end stations still gouged, even with the flat centred on the seam.\n\nThe wrap now refuses by name a work whose seam is not turned\n(rotary_seam::refuse_feature_on_seam): the facets straddling the branch\nmust stand on exactly two meridian columns of one profile. Placements clear\nof the seam wrap as before, with no cut tip inside the true cross-section.\nSlivers are also skipped by the curtains as refuse_open skips them.\n\nPinned by rotary_dflat::an_off_centre_flat_across_the_seam_never_puts_a_tip_in_the_part\n(phi -pi/2 +-0.4, +-0.7, centred, midway; n 16/64; D2/D0.8). The seam\npins now assert the named refusal.\n\nRefs #54\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
